Ollama vs Open source

    Ollama
        It's like a software product which runs on our machine, we don't get to run an code of it. It's like
        a application. It's able to take files which are efficiently packed models like gemma or llama. They have
        packaged these files called gguf file and it run it with efficient c++ code

    Open source:
        We get access to the actual code, the actual python code. We can run the model ourselves in IDE. We can changes
        the code, we can swap layers in Neural Networks and we can play around.

        We can also do fine tuning on these.

-------------------
Some libraries

    1. hub
        This is the library that let's you connect to the hugging face hub to download the models, datasets.
    2. datasets
        when you connect to hub and download the dataset then that dataset will become the part of this library.
        Each object represent a dataset
    3. transformers
        Transformers library let's you say. I want this model, and I want code for it.
        I want to able to run it, I can train it or do anything with it. This library will help you do all those.
    4. peft -> parameter efficient fine tuning
        It's a way to able to train our model and not required to teek the; e.g 8B parameters. We can do a more
        efficient way and this peft library will help use to do it.
    5. trl -> transformers reinforcement learning
        training transformers
    6. accelerate
        This will allow use to use to distribute models across multiple GPUs

